{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_243FL0hlDeLxjVr9krKJLd4q","content":"1\t# kredito\n2\t\n3\tFlutter app (iOS + Android) for a consumer loan broker. The user registers\n4\twith an email and a phone number, picks the amount they want to borrow, accepts\n5\tthe terms and gets a list of offers from partner banks. Two screens so far:\n6\t`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart` and `lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`.\n7\t\n8\tAnalytics is PostHog (`posthog_flutter`), set up in `lib/analytics.dart` and\n9\t`lib/main.dart`; screen views come from `PosthogObserver`. We are on the\n10\tPostHog free tier. Product events are defined in `docs/EVENTS.md`; the\n11\tscreens do not send any of them yet. Send events through `Analytics.capture`\n12\tso the key and host stay in one place."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_TYITp64u1UL5Jn8vsCB9MLJF","content":"1\t# Product events — registration funnel\n2\t\n3\tOwner: product. Status: approved, waiting for implementation.\n4\t\n5\tWe want to see where people drop out between opening the app and reading the\n6\toffers. Each row is one event. Names are snake_case and must match exactly,\n7\tdashboards and funnels are already built on them.\n8\t\n9\t| Event | When | Properties |\n10\t|---|---|---|\n11\t| `registration_email_started` | User started typing their email | — |\n12\t| `registration_phone_started` | User started typing their phone number | — |\n13\t| `loan_amount_changed` | User moved the loan amount slider | `amount` (int, the chosen amount) |\n14\t| `terms_accepted` | User ticked the terms and conditions checkbox | — |\n15\t| `registration_continue_tapped` | User tapped Continue on the registration screen | `amount` (int), `terms` (bool) |\n16\t| `offers_scrolled` | User scrolled the offers list | `offset` (double, how far they scrolled) |\n17\t\n18\tNotes\n19\t- Do not send the email or the phone number as properties (PII).\n20\t- Screen views are already tracked automatically, no event needed for those.\n21\t- The funnel is: email started → phone started → amount changed → terms\n22\t  accepted → continue tapped → offers scrolled."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_GHc1xvJs5vSVBZFyIVF0MR8E","content":"1\timport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n2\t\n3\t/// Thin wrapper around PostHog so the key and host live in one place.\n4\tclass Analytics {\n5\t  static Future<void> init() async {\n6\t    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\n7\t    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\n8\t    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n9\t    await Posthog().setup(config);\n10\t  }\n11\t\n12\t  /// Sends one event. [props] is optional.\n13\t  static Future<void> capture(String event, [Map<String, Object>? props]) =>\n14\t      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\n15\t}"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_qA5ZfKCb0Zljw5cM4q52MAQR","content":"1\timport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n2\timport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n3\t\n4\timport 'analytics.dart';\n5\timport 'screens/offer_screen.dart';\n6\timport 'screens/registration_screen.dart';\n7\t\n8\tFuture<void> main() async {\n9\t  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();\n10\t  await Analytics.init();\n11\t  runApp(const KreditoApp());\n12\t}\n13\t\n14\tclass KreditoApp extends StatelessWidget {\n15\t  const KreditoApp({super.key});\n16\t\n17\t  @override\n18\t  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n19\t    return PostHogWidget(\n20\t      child: MaterialApp(\n21\t        title: 'Kredito',\n22\t        theme: ThemeData(colorSchemeSeed: Colors.green, useMaterial3: true),\n23\t        navigatorObservers: [PosthogObserver()],\n24\t        routes: {\n25\t          '/': (_) => const RegistrationScreen(),\n26\t          '/offers': (_) => const OfferScreen(),\n27\t        },\n28\t      ),\n29\t    );\n30\t  }\n31\t}"}
